# meta_wearables_dat_flutter — Cursor rules (1.0)

> Canonical context: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). This is a condensed copy.
> Meta DAT reference: <https://wearables.developer.meta.com/llms.txt?full=true>

Unofficial Flutter plugin (iSee Labs, MIT), version **1.0.0** on Meta
Wearables DAT **1.0.0**. Not affiliated with Meta. Plugin `major.minor`
tracks DAT; `@experimental` APIs are outside semver.

## Architecture

- Dart facade `lib/meta_wearables_dat_flutter.dart` (static
  `MetaWearablesDat`), sealed `DatError`, models in `lib/src/models/**`,
  `lib/experimental.dart` for experimental models.
- `lib/src/channels.dart` is the only source of channel names:
  MethodChannel `meta_wearables_dat_flutter` (67 methods) + 34
  EventChannels `meta_wearables_dat_flutter/<name>`.
- Native bridges with matching type names on iOS
  (`ios/meta_wearables_dat_flutter/Sources/meta_wearables_dat_flutter/`) and
  Android (`android/src/main/kotlin/com/iseelabs/meta_wearables_dat_flutter/`):
  `MetaWearablesDatPlugin`, `WireCodec`, `DeviceSessionHub`,
  `MetaSessionManager`, `MetaDisplayManager`, `DisplayNode`,
  `MetaMockDeviceManager`, `DeviceStateObserver`, `RegistrationBridge`,
  `ResourceLedger`, `EventSinkHandler`.
- Links 7 DAT modules: Core (incl. voice invocations), Camera, Display,
  MockDevice, Inputs, Motion, Speech (last three experimental).
- One shared `DeviceSession` per device (`DeviceSessionHub`
  acquire/release) for camera, display and experimental capabilities.

## Event channels (34)

`registration_state`, `registration_errors`, `registration_requests`,
`active_device`, `devices`, `device_state`, `compatibility`,
`device_session_state`, `device_session_errors`, `stream_session_state`,
`stream_session_errors`, `camera_state`, `video_stream_size`,
`video_frames`, `audio_frames`, `photo_state`, `photo_progress`,
`photo_errors`, `display_state`, `display_events`, `display_errors`,
`inputs_state`, `inputs_events`, `inputs_errors`, `motion_state`,
`motion_samples`, `motion_errors`, `speech_state`,
`speech_transcriptions`, `speech_errors`, `voice_invocations`,
`voice_state`, `voice_errors`, `mock_devices`.

## Wire contract v2 and errors

- State channels carry strings and replay the last value.
- Method errors: `PlatformException(code: CATEGORY, details: {case,
  description, platformCase, platform})`; event errors `{code: case,
  category, message, platformCase, platform}`.
- `DatError`: `category`, `code`, typed `reason`, `platformCase`,
  `recoveryAction`. Subclasses per area (`StreamError`,
  `DeviceSessionError`, `DisplayError`, ...), plus `DatArgumentError` and
  `DatPluginError` (`EXPERIMENTAL_NOT_LINKED`).

## Toolchain

Flutter >= 3.44, Dart ^3.8, Xcode 26.4+, iOS 17.2, **SPM only** (no
CocoaPods). Android minSdk 31, compileSdk 36, Kotlin 2.2.21, AGP 8.11.1,
JVM 17, artifacts on **Maven Central** (no GitHub Packages, no token).
`MainActivity` extends `FlutterFragmentActivity`. Android
`mwdat.experimental=false` drops Inputs/Motion/Speech; iOS always links them.

## Conventions

- Dart: `very_good_analysis`, `flutter analyze --fatal-infos` clean,
  dartdoc on every public symbol, `@experimental` where applicable,
  `Future<T>`/`Stream<T>` only.
- Swift: `async`/`await`, `AnyListenerToken.cancel()`, `@MainActor` for
  channel/UI code.
- Kotlin: `Flow`/`StateFlow` + `collectLatest`, scope per capability
  cancelled in `stop*`. SDK packages `com.meta.wearable.dat.*`.

## Hard rules

- Texture path never sends frames over MethodChannel; `videoFramesStream`
  opt-in and subscriber-gated; sinks set in `onListen`, nulled in
  `onCancel`; `stopStreamSession()` unregisters the texture and the
  `ResourceLedger` returns to zero.
- Android `StateFlow`s start at `STOPPED`; never treat the initial value
  as terminal.
- Public Dart streams: no `async*` with awaited teardown.
- Add a channel in Dart + Swift + Kotlin together; keep
  `dart run tool/check_channel_parity.dart` green.
- Android display builders: named arguments. Never call Android
  `display.stop()`; use `session.removeDisplay()`.
- iOS `IconName` raw values are snake_case; Dart `DisplayIconName` is
  camelCase.
- Swift XCTest only on iOS 26+ simulators.
- When uncertain about Meta SDK behavior, stop and ask.

## Naming map

| Meta | Dart |
|---|---|
| `Wearables` | `MetaWearablesDat` |
| `DeviceSession` | shared via `DeviceSessionHub` |
| `StreamConfiguration` / `StreamSessionConfig` | `StreamSessionConfig` |
| `AutoDeviceSelector` / `SpecificDeviceSelector` | default / `deviceUUID:` |
| `Display` DSL `FlexBox/Text/Image/Button/ButtonGroup/Icon/VideoPlayer` | `FlexBox/DisplayText/DisplayImage/DisplayButton/DisplayButtonGroup/DisplayIcon/VideoPlayer` |
| `MockDeviceKit` | `enableMockDevice()` / `*Mock*()` |

